In this file you will find details about how I implemented the first task_case01

This case verifies if users with different roles can log in.
BaseTest: it starts the browser. I have selected @BeforeMethod because each role has its own permissions and each role must be logged in separately
(not in one session).

LoginTest verifies such things:
1. Admin role has specific elements: users item in the left menu and this role also has refresh item in the upper left corner
In test for this role I have verified if both elements (described above) are displayed and to prove that user logged it successfully - the dashboard page should be opened.
**Admin role has users item in the left menu and refresh item in the upper left corner**
2. Subscriber role - very very simple role: there are no particular characteristics that would set this role apart. There are only 2 items in the left menu that are available for all other roles.
so I have decided that if this role does NOT have items for other roles that meant - that it is this role.
**Subscriber - has NO Posts, NO Media, NO users **
3. Contributor role - has Posts, NO Media , NO users, NO pages
4. Author role - has Posts, has Media , NO users, NO pages
5. Editor role - has Posts, has Media , NO users, has pages

Also I have added listeners, added priority for login tests.

